      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Bell Theorem rigorously tests the compatibility of quantum mechanics with the concept of local realism. Local realism posits that physical properties exist independently of measurement (realism) and that no influence can travel faster than the speed of light (locality). Bell derived mathematical inequalities (Bell inequalities) that any theory obeying local realism must satisfy. Experimental violations of these inequalities, such as those seen in entangled particle measurements, decisively rule out the possibility of hidden variables preserving both locality and realism simultaneously.",
